    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179-a4">

                <pb facs="0352" n="1006" xml:id="pg1006"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 to No. 14.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gibbs to Captain
                            Johnson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 11,
                        1875</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received the inclosed communication
                    from the minister of foreign relations,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d179-f1"/> of which
                    I send you copy and translation. An aid-de-camp of the President of the republic
                    has also called on me to offer his regrets at the great loss we all have
                    experienced.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, your obedient servant.</p>
                <closer><signed>RICHARD GIBBS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Captain <hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip C. Johnson</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Commanding United States Flag-ship Richmond, Callao
                            Bay.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
